===== 8729 Page 251
8 P. M. 13th  Macon Ga. May 11 1865
2 P. M. 11th Genl Thomas Telegrams of the 7th & 9th recd
with the light draft boats now on the Savannah & one or
two that maybe got from the Alatamaha the supplies
necessary for my command ought to be got to Augusta from
there can bring by R. R. ----- With money I could 
purchase forage for twenty or twenty five days longer in
South west Georgia at present by Command's distributed over a
wide area country stretching from Etowah to Tallahassie &
subsistence by forced purchase upon the country , we
may be able there by get few days grain ahead provisions are
already arriving from Savannah , have 15 days besides already 
here ---- Our horses are suffering want hay , grass
this region very hurtful to them & but little
corn fodder to be had . on receipt of letter from
Steedman few days ago saying he had begun <insertion>repairing</insertion> Chattanooga
& Atlanta RR I began operations from this End ,
they say bridge already framed for Chattahoochee , I have 
3,000 negro troops who could be put work &
Genl Winslow thinks whole road can be rebuilt in twenty
days it would do good to cause pacification to
rebuild the RR - Savannah & Ocmulgee rivers cannot be 
relied upon for great while shall I continue the work ?
? can fill our wagon trains with " C. S. A "
cotton , besides that there are 50 thousand bales in 
ware house here claimed by private citizens Shall I do

===== 10302 Page 160
7 P. M. Cairo Ill May 6. 1864 
Cairo May 5th Midnight for Secy of Navy ---- The Eastport sunk
by a torpedo on the fifteenth Apl was raised &
after great toil removed down the river fifty two miles
where finding her immovably fixed on a bed of logs
she was blown up on the twenty sixth sixty miles
above Alexandria which our army has already reached guns &
stores saved ---- Cricket flag Ship Hindman Juliet & two
pump boats were with her ---- We were attacked by
fifteen hundred Infy as train was about being fired ----
Enemy attempted to board Cricket but was driven off after
short engagement ---- their loss unknown ours four wounded ----
Eastport was then fired by Capt Phelps & reduced to
complete wreck ---- Laid by her two hours then proceeded
down river ---- ten miles below were opened on by
a battery of fifteen's twenty fours & twelves supported by
large Infy force ---- Cricket passed battery with loss of
twenty five killed thirteen wounded out of crew of fifty
---- was struck thirty eight times ---- shot & shell
in four minutes besides heavy musketry the one pump boat 
exploded in boiler drifted under battery & abandoned by crew
---- Juliet in tow of another pump boat was disabled
& backed up out of fire covered by Hindman ----
Cricket grounded below & set on fire by Explosion of
ammunition ---- Fire extinguished without serious damage ---- Hindman &
Juliet repaired damages during night & next day with remaining

